  "releaseNotes": "Add\n      - PropertyChangedTrackingEventHandler, PropertyChangedTrackingEventArgs\n      Modify\n      - The PropertyChangedTracker can change how it determines the value to track by overriding GetPropertyValue().\n      - PropertyChangedTracker has been modified to raise the OnResetCompleted() and ResetCompleted events when Reset() is performed.\n      - PropertyChangedTracker has been modified to raise the OnTrackingPropertyValueChanged() and TrackingPropertyValueChanged events when TrackingProperty() is performed.\n      - PropertyChangedTracker's ContainsChangedProperty() has been replaced by HasChanged().\n      - PropertyChangedTracker now has a SetInstance() method, which is useful when a constructor with arguments is not available.\n      - The TrackingObject has been modified to explicitly specify a PropertyChangeTracker.\n      - TrackingObject's OnPropertyChanged() can now be overridden.\n      - The StatefulTrackingObject has been modified to explicitly specify a PropertyChangeTracker.\n      - When a row is added using Add() or Insert(), TrackingList now adds the added item as ItemState.NotModified if the added item was ItemState.New.\n      - TrackingList no longer changes the ItemState when content within an item changes. To change the ItemState, the specified item must provide it.\n      - Improved the accuracy of Unicode detection for StringExtensions.GetTextCount() and StringExtensions.IsFullWidth().",
